					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13877208</guid>
				<title>SCP-5913</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13877208/scp-5913</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2020 15:03:43 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>WizzBlizz</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>6760712</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>very poor clinical tone.</p> <p>Some examples:</p> <blockquote> <p>SCP-5913 is a humanoid entity dressed up in a bartender suit of the 1920s</p> </blockquote> <p>It should be more specific. What is a bartender suit of the 1920s? What does that look like?</p> <blockquote> <p>subject is measuring</p> </blockquote> <p>Grammar issue here. Should be &quot;subject measures&quot;</p> <blockquote> <p>the subject shows very little muscle mass, arms are grossly out of proportion with the rest of the body, the subject has shown to have no signs of hair,</p> </blockquote> <p>should refer to the SCP rather than 'subject'. This isn't a test log.</p> <blockquote> <p>I have always observed the subject to have chief strength</p> </blockquote> <p>Why are we speaking in first person? SCP files should be written always in third person.</p> <blockquote> <p>The tendrils that SCP-5913 sprouts out from its body</p> </blockquote> <p>Should be &quot;The tendrils that sprout from SCP-5913's body.&quot; The phrasing suggests that 5913 is consciously sprouting tendrils?</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
